ple actually say, including slang and idioms."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Confidence.", "marks": [{"type": "bold"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " Using a language with a patient person is the fastest way to stop freezing up."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Culture.", "marks": [{"type": "bold"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " You learn why people say things, not just what they say."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Cost.", "marks": [{"type": "bold"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " It is free. You pay with your time and your own language."}]}]}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What it is not"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Your partner is not a teacher. They may not be able to explain "}, {"type": "text", "text": "why", "marks": [{"type": "italic"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " a grammar rule works, only that something sounds right or wrong. That is fine: pair the exchange with a course, a book or an app for structure, and use the exchange for practice."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "It is also not a dating site or a social feed. The best exchanges stay focused on helping each other learn."}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Who can take part"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Anyone. Complete beginners (CEFR level A1) can exchange too: write short messages, ask simple questions, and lean on your partner's corrections. Advanced learners (C1 and C2) use exchanges to polish style and sound natural. If you are not sure what the levels mean, they run from A1 (beginner) to C2 (near-native)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "You also do not have to be a native speaker to help. A learner at an intermediate level (B1 and above) can often correct a beginner perfectly well."}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "How to get the most out of it"}]}, {"type": "orderedList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Be specific about what you want.", "marks": [{"type": "bold"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " \"Please correct my grammar but ignore small typos\" helps your partner help you."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Show up regularly.", "marks": [{"type": "bold"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " Ten minutes most days beats two hours once a month."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Give as much as you take.", "marks": [{"type": "bold"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " The exchanges that last are the ones where both people feel helped."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Review your corrections.", "marks": [{"type": "bold"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " Look back at what you got wrong last week. That is where the learning sticks."}]}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Ready to try one? Read "}, {"type": "text", "text": "how to find a language exchange partner online", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "/blog/find-a-language-exchange-partner"}}]}, {"type": "text", "text": ", or see "}, {"type": "text", "text": "how to ask native speakers for corrections", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "/blog/corrections-from-native-speakers"}}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " without feeling awkward."}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "How The Fluency Talks does it"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "On "}, {"type": "text", "text": "The Fluency Talks", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "/"}}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " you choose the language you speak and the one you are learning, and we show you every native speaker of your target language plus everyone learning yours. A perfect swap ranks first, but you never need one. You chat in writing, and your partner can correct a sentence right where you wrote it. You see exactly what changed, accept it or not, and accepted corrections go into your own phrasebook to review later. It is free, with no paid plans."}]}]}$j$::jsonb, 6, '2026-11-01 10:00+00', '2026-11-01 10:00+00', '2026-11-01 10:00+00', '2026-11-01 10:00+00');
insert into public.blog_posts (slug, draft, is_live, title, seo_title, description, kicker, summary, body, read_minutes, published_at, updated_at, created_at, draft_saved_at) values (
  'find-a-language-exchange-partner', $j${"title": "How to Find a Language Exchange Partner Online (Free)", "seo_title": "Find a Free Language Exchange Partner Online", "description": "Where to find a language exchange partner online for free, what to look for in a good match, and what to write in your first message so they say yes.", "kicker": "Getting started", "summary": "The quickest way to find a language exchange partner is to look for a native speaker of the language you are learning, or a learner of the language you speak. Someone who is both is a bonus, not a requirement. Use a platform that matches by language pair, write a short, specific first message, and agree early on how often you will talk.", "body": {"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Start with the right match"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "You do not need a perfect mirror. If you speak English and are learning Vietnamese, any native Vietnamese speaker can help you, even one who is learning nothing, and you can help anyone who is learning English, even a French speaker. A native Vietnamese speaker who is also learning English is the ideal pair, because each of you has a reason to keep showing up, but waiting for one slows you down."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Three things matter more than anything else:"}]}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The language pair.", "marks": [{"type": "bold"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " Someone speaks what you are learning, or is learning what you speak. Both at once is a bonus."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A similar level.", "marks": [{"type": "bold"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " Not identical, but if one person is at A1 and the other at C1, conversations tend to drift into one language."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Similar availability.", "marks": [{"type": "bold"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " Time zones matter less for text chat, but you still need to reply within a day or two."}]}]}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Where to look"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "You have a few kinds of options, all free:"}]}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Language exchange apps and sites.", "marks": [{"type": "bold"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " These are built for exactly this, and the good ones match you by language rather than by photos or follower counts."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Local meetups and university groups.", "marks": [{"type": "bold"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " Many universities run tandem programmes, and cities often have language cafés."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Online communities.", "marks": [{"type": "bold"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " Language-learning forums and subreddits often have partner-finding threads. Be specific about your languages and level."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "People you already know.", "marks": [{"type": "bold"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " A colleague or classmate who grew up speaking another language may be glad to help, and you can help them back."}]}]}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What to look for in a profile"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Before you message someone, check that they have filled in their languages and level, and that they say what they want from an exchange. Someone who writes \"I want to practise everyday English for work\" is easier to help, and more likely to reply, than an empty profile."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Fill in your own profile the same way. It is the first thing a potential partner sees."}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What to write in your first message"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Keep it short and give them something to answer. A good first message has four parts: hello, who you are, what you want, and a question."}]}, {"type": "blockquote", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Hi Linh! I'm Tom, a native English speaker learning Vietnamese (about A2). "}, {"type": "text", "text": "Rất vui được làm quen!", "marks": [{"type": "lang", "attrs": {"lang": "vi"}}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " I'd love to practise a few times a week by chat, and I'm happy to help with your English. What made you start learning English?"}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Avoid long life stories, copy-pasted messages to dozens of people, and anything that is not about learning. And write part of the message in the language you are learning, even if it is just one sentence, like Tom's "}, {"type": "text", "text": "\"Rất vui được làm quen!\"", "marks": [{"type": "italic"}, {"type": "lang", "attrs": {"lang": "vi"}}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " (\"Nice to meet you!\"). It shows effort."}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Agree on how you will work"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "After the first few messages, settle two questions:"}]}, {"type": "orderedList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "How will you split the languages?", "marks": [{"type": "bold"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " Alternate days, half and half, or each person writes in the language they are learning."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "How do you want to be corrected?", "marks": [{"type": "bold"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " Every mistake, or only the important ones? Read "}, {"type": "text", "text": "how to ask for corrections", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "/blog/corrections-from-native-speakers"}}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " for wording that works."}]}]}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Staying safe"}]}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Keep the conversation on the platform until you trust the person."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Do not share your address, financial details or passwords."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "If someone makes you uncomfortable, stop replying, block them and report them. A good platform makes this easy."}]}]}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "If a partner goes quiet"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "It happens, and it is rarely personal: people get busy. Send one friendly follow-up, then move on. It is normal to message several people before one exchange really clicks, and many learners keep two or three partners going at once."}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Finding a partner on The Fluency Talks"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "On "}, {"type": "text", "text": "The Fluency Talks", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "/"}}]}, {"type": "text", "text": ", you pick your native language and the language and level you are learning, and you see native speakers of your target language and learners of yours, ranked by language and not by popularity. A perfect swap comes first but is never required. New contacts arrive as requests that the other person can accept or decline, and you can block or report anyone. It is free: "}, {"type": "text", "text": "create an account", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "/signup"}}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " and send your first message today."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "New to the idea? Start with "}, {"type": "text", "text": "what a language exchange is and how it works", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "/blog/what-is-a-language-exchange"}}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "."}]}]}, "cover_url": null, "cover_alt": null}$j$::jsonb, true,
  $t$How to Find a Language Exchange Partner Online (Free)$t$, $t$Find a Free Language Exchange Partner Online$t$, $t$Where to find a language exchange partner online for free, what to look for in a good match, and what to write in your first message so they say yes.$t$, $t$Getting started$t$, $t$The quickest way to find a language exchange partner is to look for a native speaker of the language you are learning, or a learner of the language you speak. Someone who is both is a bonus, not a requirement. Use a platform that matches by language pair, write a short, specific first message, and agree early on how often you will talk.$t$,
