tItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Keep the conversation on the platform until you trust the person."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Do not share your address, financial details or passwords."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "If someone makes you uncomfortable, stop replying, block them and report them. A good platform makes this easy."}]}]}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "If a partner goes quiet"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "It happens, and it is rarely personal: people get busy. Send one friendly follow-up, then move on. It is normal to message several people before one exchange really clicks, and many learners keep two or three partners going at once."}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Finding a partner on The Fluency Talks"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "On "}, {"type": "text", "text": "The Fluency Talks", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "/"}}]}, {"type": "text", "text": ", you pick your native language and the language and level you are learning, and you see native speakers of your target language and learners of yours, ranked by language and not by popularity. A perfect swap comes first but is never required. New contacts arrive as requests that the other person can accept or decline, and you can block or report anyone. It is free: "}, {"type": "text", "text": "create an account", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "/signup"}}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " and send your first message today."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "New to the idea? Start with "}, {"type": "text", "text": "what a language exchange is and how it works", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {