eep what you learn"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A correction you read once and never see again is mostly lost. Write each one down with the wrong and the right version side by side, add an example or a picture if it helps you remember, and look back over the list once a week. Patterns appear quickly: you will notice you always get the same preposition wrong, and then you will stop."}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "How corrections work on The Fluency Talks"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "On "}, {"type": "text", "text": "The Fluency Talks", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "/"}}]}, {"type": "text", "text": ", correcting is built into the chat. A native speaker, or a learner at B1 or above, edits your sentence right where you wrote it. You see what you wrote in red and the correction in green, and you choose whether to accept it. Accepted corrections are saved to your personal phrasebook, so reviewing them is one tap away."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "People who correct you earn 5 points for each correction you accept, so helping is rewarded. And if you are stuck on a question, you can spend 50 points on a bounty to show it to people who know the language. The helper gets the 50 points when you accept their answer; if you accept none within 48 hours, you get them back."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Still looking for someone to practise with? Here is "}, {"type": "text", "text": "how to find a language exchange partner online", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "/blog/find-a-language-exchange-partner"}}]}, {"type": "text", "text": ", or "}, {"type": "text", "text": "sign up free", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "/signup"}}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " and get matched today."}]}]}$j$::jsonb, 6, '2026-11-01 12:00+00', '2026-11-01 12:00+00', '202